  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Desk at Home",
    "overview": "The identity is one illustration: a developer's desk in a Bangladeshi home, with a laptop typing its own code, a glass of cha that steams and can be sipped, a red khata and pen, a lamp, plants, a bookshelf, and a window onto a coconut palm under sun or moon. The desk sits full width at the top of the home page on a band of soft wall blue. Everything below it is quiet: warm paper background, deep ink text, pink section headings, blue for subtitles and hover. The page reads like a person's notebook, not a product launch.\n\nDensity is relaxed. Content sits in one centred column up to 1080px, split into a wide project column and a narrower sidebar on desktop. Playfulness lives in two places only: the desk scene, and the small spring overshoot when you hover a link arrow, a pill, a button, or the theme toggle. Night mode is part of the world, not a filter: the lamp beam comes on, stars appear in the window, the sun turns into a moon, and the wood and wall go dark.\n\nThe user rejected 3D, a terminal look, and anything that resembles a mobile-app landing page. The friendly tone takes after joshwcomeau.com without copying it.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One illustrated desk scene as the identity; the rest of the page stays plain and readable.",
      "Two full palettes (day and night), both set as custom properties and switched by `data-theme` on the root.",
      "A single sans family (Figtree) used at heavy weights for headings, with Hind Siliguri for বাংলা.",
      "Pink headings, blue secondary text and hover states, ink body copy.",
      "Flat surfaces. Depth comes from soft tinted fills and hairline edges.",
      "Spring-eased hover feedback; all ambient motion stays inside the desk."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Two Palettes Rule",
        "body": "Every color a surface uses must be a custom property with both a day value on `:root` and a night value on `:root[data-theme=\"dark\"]`. Hard-coded colors are allowed only for fixed objects inside the illustration (books, plants, khata, laptop screen code).",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Pink Is For Headings Rule",
        "body": "Pink marks section headings and small identity details (wordmark dot, বাংলা, list markers). Blue handles interaction. Don't swap them.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Family Rule",
        "body": "Hierarchy comes from Figtree's weight (400 to 800) and size alone. No uppercase labels, no letter-spaced eyebrows, no second display face.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Bangla Gets Its Own Face Rule",
        "body": "Any বাংলা text is marked `lang=\"bn\"` and set in Hind Siliguri at 600.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Paper Rule",
        "body": "Cards, pills, buttons and code chips never cast shadows. The only shadow is the soft lift under a product screenshot.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** keep the desk scene as the one illustrated moment, and repaint any new scene element through day/night custom properties.",
      "**Do** define every new UI color as a token on both `:root` and `:root[data-theme=\"dark\"]`.",
      "**Do** use the `--spring` linear() curve (0.4 to 0.6s) for hover feedback on arrows, pills, buttons and toggles.",
      "**Do** end onward links with the 16px line arrow that slides 5px on hover.",
      "**Do** set section headings in Figtree 800 in pink, with a plain, conversational phrase.",
      "**Do** mark Bangla with `lang=\"bn\"` and set it in Hind Siliguri 600.",
      "**Do** keep prose in soft ink at 58 to 64ch."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** add ambient motion outside the desk scene; page content never animates into view.",
      "**Don't** add shadows to cards, pills or buttons; the product screenshot is the only lifted object.",
      "**Don't** add 3D, terminal styling, or mobile-app-landing-page heroes (rejected by the user).",
      "**Don't** add uppercase eyebrows or kicker labels above headings.",
      "**Don't** use pink for link or hover states in page UI, or blue for headings.",
      "**Don't** let motion hide content; under reduced motion everything must render in its final state."
    ]
  }
